.superpowers/
.viva/
.gg/

# Python bytecode — never tracked; a test run would otherwise dirty the tree
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Transient story scaffolding — a design doc and its build plan live in the
# branch until the story ships, then disappear with the worktree. What survives
# lands in PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md, CLAUDE.md, or docs/headless-contract.md; the
# decision itself lives in the issue.
docs/design/
PLAN.md
# …except the parse fixture of that name. A pathless `PLAN.md` matches at any
# depth, so without this negation `tests/fixtures/PLAN.md` is ignored — it only
# survives today because it is already tracked, and a delete-and-re-add would
# silently drop it and break `test_parse_sections.py` on a fresh clone.
!tests/fixtures/PLAN.md
